    h1: "NFL Teaser Picks 2026 - Free Expert Teasers & Strategy",
    body: "\n<p>NFL teasers are one of the smartest tools in a football bettor's arsenal when used correctly, and this page delivers free expert teaser picks plus the strategy behind them all 2026 season. A teaser lets you adjust the point spread in your favor across two or more games in exchange for a lower payout. The standard NFL teaser moves the line six points, which can turn a tricky spread into a much more comfortable number. Combine our teaser plays with our <a href=\"/picks/nfl-picks/\">free NFL picks</a> for a well-rounded card.</p>\n<h2>How NFL Teasers Work</h2>\n<p>In a six-point teaser, you select two or more teams and shift each spread six points in your favor. For example, a team favored by 7.5 becomes favored by just 1.5, and an underdog getting 2.5 now gets 8.5. All teased legs must win for the teaser to pay, similar to a parlay but with the added cushion of the adjusted line. The payout is lower than a standard parlay because you are buying those extra points, but the improved probability often makes teasers a strong value.</p>\n<h2>The Key to Teaser Strategy: Key Numbers</h2>\n<p>The most important concept in NFL teaser betting is crossing the key numbers of 3 and 7, the two most common margins of victory in the NFL. The classic profitable teaser, often called the Wong teaser, involves teasing favorites of 7.5 to 8.5 down through both 7 and 3, or teasing underdogs of 1.5 to 2.5 up through 3 and 7. Moving through both key numbers dramatically improves your odds because so many NFL games land on those exact margins. This is why disciplined teaser bettors focus on specific spread ranges rather than teasing any game.</p>\n<h2>Our NFL Teaser Approach</h2>\n<p>We post teaser picks that target these key-number spots, favoring two-team six-point teasers built on spreads in the optimal ranges. We avoid teasing totals or crossing zero key numbers, and we steer clear of large multi-leg teasers that erode the mathematical edge. For pure parlay action, see our <a href=\"/picks/nfl-parlay-picks/\">NFL parlay picks</a>, and for single-game combinations check our <a href=\"/picks/nfl-same-game-parlay/\">NFL same game parlay</a> page.</p>\n<h2>Teaser Betting Tips</h2>\n<p>Stick to two-team teasers through the key numbers, avoid teasing home favorites off the number just for the sake of it, and shop for the best teaser odds since they vary by sportsbook. Bookmark this page for our free NFL teaser picks throughout the 2026 season, and always bet within a disciplined bankroll.</p>\n",
